" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "77bbdf627ed7f3686453d595b16131a4b47d0ebe8f5762584f11bb2503ec45f3" "basis" 1773 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/b9364923447e278db5ec47bef74e1a05310645b30df22d4ea5efcc0de46c6ed2.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/16cb1608f70821d138f0c6984038bb42d86d9fbf76d560d94d2e25bd6fdb05e0.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0abbbaf34955fa40d6cdbfa9e16cb1567ee16271d65b4565206a0f2204eedf6d.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/4b915439c3e9922d692aab4205a728160e0a1286f82fa5ebc736460901581147.png)\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "77bbdf627ed7f3686453d595b16131a4b47d0ebe8f5762584f11bb2503ec45f3" "basis" 1773 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ z-x+2=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/0d06481c63a618262b9034124c24cd1d0c566ee9d6b891fa470e09dc67f5f6c6.png)\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "1945b607231fd354cca39cdf2ad8730c1482495d54613ff0d9eea4674befb912" "basis" 1773 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4519" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/104c591a6a72cf3caab1bc2a965c57258bb37a31578254696e0c1cd740fe5915.png)\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/e008383384401198e67f648cce33a720d98afb6a6f60a14ba7ffa21dcc095a5f.png)\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/c85e33202a691b685431ac16efab6a7fd932eac056743df6e81632587f0465b2.png)\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/assets/64d1f57717dda57c8a7fbc403728ee9699a22ce995f68a50a0b80f25543fdab6.png)\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/example-4519.json" "file_sha256" "1945b607231fd354cca39cdf2ad8730c1482495d54613ff0d9eea4674befb912" "basis" 1773 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14052721/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-316995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x=6 \\\\ 2x+z=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+0z=6 \\\\ 2x+0y+z=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316995" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $2$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $14$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $3$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-8$ | $4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-7$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+0z=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316988" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+8z=0 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z=3 \\\\ 5x-4y+7z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & a \\\\ 2 & b & 4 \\\\ 5 & c & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=8,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-2,\\,b=7,\\,c=-5"] ["math" "a=-4,\\,b=-5,\\,c=8"] ["math" "a=-4,\\,b=0,\\,c=4"] ["math" "a=3,\\,b=4,\\,c=7"] ["math" "a=8,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-36178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=8,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z=1 \\\\ y-3z=0 \\\\ 4z=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z=1 \\\\ 0x+y-3z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+4z=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-316996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"}