rrect" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & c\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+y+2z=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-1,\\,b=2,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=0,\\,b=1,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=-3"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=2,\\,c=3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-10004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-2z+x-5y=1 \\\\ -y+5z-4x=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & a \\\\ b & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & c & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-5y-2z=1 \\\\ -4x-y+5z=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z=2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-2,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6"] ["math" "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6"] ["math" "a=-5,\\,b=-1,\\,c=-6"] ["math" "a=-5,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6"] ["math" "a=5,\\,b=4,\\,c=-6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75512" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4z+x-3=7 \\\\ 2x-5y+6=1 \\\\ 3y+7z-4x+5=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $10$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $3$ | $7$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+4z=10 \\\\ 2x-5y+0z=-5 \\\\ -4x+3y+7z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-317639" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca708582