\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ b \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y+z=0 \\\\ 2x+0y+z=1 \\\\ -3x+7y-2z=0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-75513" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-75513" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Dev