}-5x-2y+2z=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-316998" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "080a90503e656a557f8dc4bec5a7dcb22b23de9ea3e46fcbb08eb0a5368c19dc"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6"] ["math" "a=-3,\\,b=5,\\,c=8"] ["math" "a=-7,\\,b=1,\\,c=1"] ["math" "a=1,\\,b=-7,\\,c=8"] ["math" "a=4,\\,b=1,\\,c=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "q-130562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/state.json" "file_sha256" "4abece85528e0cbcb171ea6eaba5a1d41b2cf9486ca70858296d13756d64527d"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y-z=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/assets/ed434344208758284aa0f144676f7dd6498a63faeb0248d18e87c4be6c3d87f2.png)\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083420/example-4518.json" "file_sha256" "248c172678329a55ddaf8d71964cea4e01352adf0530fa46e315993d6c38d41f"} {"question" "e-4518" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z=1 \\\